For M4, I’ve written the uniform tail and relative-score estimates, plus a planar Gaussian-polynomial integrability lemma. I found a useful way to handle measurability: the second heat moment is the derivative of the continuous first moment, so Mathlib’s measurable-derivative theorem applies. I’m now using these to justify differentiation of the concrete product integral.
