## P36

The exact requested theorem is incrementally kernel-checked as `ChowlaCosine.P36.p36_truncation`, with genuine `Finset ℕ`, explicit positive-frequency and `D≥1` hypotheses, and every real angle. No fallback constant was used. The sine-vector kernel has exact first coefficient `cos(pi/(D+2))`.

Also checked: `p36_gap` (same exact cosine error times `Y² * core.card`) and `p36_gap_pi` (the paper's explicit `pi²/2 * (Y/(D+2))² * core.card`). Empty cores are covered. Supporting modules: `P36/Kernel.lean`, `P36/SineKernel.lean`, `P36/Main.lean`.

