## Beckner M4

New incremental kernel-checked progress in `Beckner/HeatFlowUniform.lean` and `Beckner/HeatFlowIntegral.lean`:

- Uniform Gaussian tails for scalar heat flow and the actual geometric product on every interval `0<a≤t≤b`.
- Uniform relative spatial/time-score bounds and a Gaussian-polynomial bound on the actual product time derivative.
- Spatial continuity of heat flow/first moments; measurability of second moments and time scores via their actual derivative formulas.
- Whole-plane integrability of `(1+x²+y²) exp(-d(x²+y²))` for every `d>0`.
- `integrable_geometricHeatProduct_plane` for the actual product in coordinates of any two-dimensional orthonormal basis.
- `hasDerivAt_integral_geometricHeatProduct_plane`: concrete differentiation under the whole-plane integral, with all local uniform domination, measurability, and integrability hypotheses supplied for nonnegative interval-supported L1 data of positive mass.

The spatial derivative assembly is now incrementally kernel-checked in `HeatFlowSpatial.lean` and `HeatFlowMonotone.lean`. Both actual spatial slopes are measurable and integrable on the whole plane; the first slope has the stated second-slope derivative along every affine line. `geometricHeatProduct_integral_derivative_nonneg` instantiates `parabolic_integral_derivative_nonneg` with all hypotheses supplied. `geometricHeatProduct_integral_monotone` proves monotonicity of the actual whole-plane geometric-product integral on all positive times for the stated compact-data stage. This closes the prior report's obligation 1. Next: rescaled large-time limit. Rescaled large-time limit, initial-time passage, density extension, and sharp-factor change of variables remain open. These intermediate support hypotheses have not been passed off as a complete arbitrary-data sharp Young theorem. No sharp Young/M5/P31-N completion is claimed. The ordinary build through `HeatFlowIntegral.lean` passed (8714 jobs). The spatial/monotonicity file build and complete axiom audit remain pending.


